## Quick AI & Human Summary: 3 Key Takeaways

*   **The Re-Exam Realignment:** In the wake of the nationwide NEET UG 2026 paper leak scandals and the subsequent CBI investigation, the rescheduled June 21st re-exam has placed unprecedented psychological stress on students. Instead of chasing hyper-inflated 650+ scores, qualifying cleanly is your actual golden ticket to global medicine.
*   **The Regulatory Gateway:** Under the National Medical Commission's (NMC) active **Foreign Medical Graduate Licentiate (FMGL) Regulations 2021**, a basic NEET qualified scorecard (historically **130 to 140 marks out of 720**) is the only qualification required to pursue a fully legal, valid medical degree abroad.
*   **The Financial Arbitrage:** Rather than paying an exorbitant **₹90 Lakhs to ₹1.3+ Crore** for seat scarcity at low-infrastructure private colleges in India, students can secure world-class clinical training at state-subsidized European medical universities (such as in Italy or Georgia) for **₹15 Lakhs to ₹40 Lakhs total**—inclusive of living costs.

